# Implement the local MCP transport

## Goal

Expose accepted capabilities to Codex and other MCP clients without adding an
unnecessary public service boundary.

## Required work

- Implement stdio transport as the default.
- Advertise schemas and annotations from one contract source.
- Add capability configuration that fails closed.
- Keep protocol output separate from diagnostics.
- Document Codex configuration and lifecycle.

## Acceptance criteria

- No TCP listener starts by default.
- Stdout contains MCP frames only.
- Disabled tools are absent, not merely rejected after invocation.
- A protocol conformance test exercises initialization and representative tools.

## Evidence

- MCP client integration test
- Example Codex configuration without secrets
